 *
 * @page culite_tutorial_eigsol Eigenvalue Solvers
 *
 * cuLite provides GPU-accelerated eigenvalue solvers for dense matrices, utilizing
 * optimized cuSOLVER backends.
 *
 * - @subpage culite_tutorial_eigsol_geev
 *
 * @page culite_tutorial_eigsol_geev General Eigenvalue Problem (GEEV)
 *
 * This section demonstrates how to compute eigenvalues and eigenvectors of general
 * (non-symmetric) dense matrices on GPU using the GEEV algorithm.
 * Eigenvalues are returned as complex values, even for real input matrices.
 * Optionally, left and/or right eigenvectors can be computed.
 * <table>
 *   <tr><th>Source Code</th><th>Console Output</th></tr>
 *   <tr>
 *     <td> @include src/ex07a_eigenproblem_geev.cpp </td>
 *     <td> @include i32/out/ex07a_eigenproblem_geev.out </td>
 *   </tr>
 * </table>
 *
 *
 *
 *
 *
 *
 * @page culite_tutorial_svd Singular Value Decomposition
 *
 * cuLite provides GPU-accelerated SVD solvers for dense matrices, utilizing
 * optimized cuSOLVER backends.
 *
 * - @subpage culite_tutorial_svd_default
 *
 * @page culite_tutorial_svd_default Default SVD
 *
 * This section demonstrates how to compute the singular value decomposition (SVD)
 * of a dense matrix on GPU. The SVD factorizes A = U * S * V*, where S contains
 * the singular values in descending order.
 * Policies control whether left (U) and right (V) singular vectors are computed.
 * Available policies are `Limited` (economy SVD), `Full`, and `NoCalculation`.
 * <table>
 *   <tr><th>Source Code</th><th>Console Output</th></tr>
 *   <tr>
 *     <td> @include src/ex08a_sv_decomposition.cpp </td>
 *     <td> @include i32/out/ex08a_sv_decomposition.out </td>
 *   </tr>
 * </table>
 */

